{"text": "JUNIPER MESA OUTFITTERS, INC.\nMEMORANDUM\n\nTO:      Hank Dellaria, CPA, and Lucinda Whitcombe, CPA -- Whitcombe Dellaria LLP\nFROM:    Rosalyn Tsosie-Baker, Controller (rtsosiebaker@junipermesa.example, 928-555-0115)\nDATE:    January 23, 2026\nRE:      FY2025 year-end close -- open items before you start fieldwork Feb. 9\n\nHank -- here is everything I know of that is unusual in the 12/31/2025 close,\nin trial balance order. The TB, bank recs and subledgers are in the shared\nfolder. Call my cell (928.555.0170) rather than the store line; I am only in\nFlagstaff Tuesday through Thursday.\n\n1. CASH\nOperating account at Ponderosa National Bank (acct ending 3318): book balance\n$214,907.33, reconciled. Four checks over 90 days outstanding, total\n$3,412.00; the largest is ck #20841 for $1,950.00 to the\nCoconino Trail Runners Association (race sponsorship) -- they say they never\ngot it. I will void and reissue in January.\nPayroll account (Ponderosa, ending 3326): $18,220.14. Reconciled to zero\nafter the 1/2/2026 payroll cleared.\nMoney market at Kaibab Credit Union, member no. 0061-4472: $402,655.80\nincluding $1,318.44 December dividend that I accrued.\nTallyho Payments (card processor) had $27,364.19 in transit at year end; it\nsettled 1/3/2026 and 1/5/2026. One chargeback of $1,286.00 is still in dispute\n(customer card ending 4609, a guided-trip deposit).\nFYI the online banking user ID is jmo_controller and the token PIN is\n7731 -- Lucinda asked for read-only access last year; please ask\nPonderosa for your own login this time rather than using mine.\n\n2. ACCOUNTS RECEIVABLE\nTotal AR $61,480.25. Almost all is wholesale/guide accounts. The one\nproblem is Red Rock Guide Service L.L.C., $14,300.00, now 140 days. The\nowner told Grant in November that he is filing Chapter 7. I reserved\n100%. Allowance otherwise unchanged at $2,500.\n\n3. INVENTORY\nPhysical count was January 4, 2026 at all three stores (Flagstaff, Sedona,\nPrescott). Count sheets signed by store managers; Jordan Yazzie ran Sedona.\nBook-to-physical shrink was $11,902 ($7,640 of it in Sedona -- see item 9).\nEnding inventory at FIFO cost $1,184,266. In-transit: one container of\ntents from Bergkamm Zelte GmbH, invoice BZ-2025-11873, EUR terms, title passed\nat Hamburg 12/18/2025, so it is in inventory at $88,415 (81,200 EUR at the\nspot rate). We paid Bergkamm on 1/14/2026 by wire to IBAN\nDE22 4140 0286 5096 1416 77, so it is in AP at year end.\n\n4. FIXED ASSETS\nAdditions, all in the fixed asset schedule:\n - 2022 Ford Transit 250 cargo van bought used 8/19/2025 for $34,750,\n   VIN 1FTBR1C82NKA40917, AZ plate CKH7R42. Financed -- see item 6.\n - Electric pallet stacker for the warehouse, serial CRW-ES4000-2291847,\n   $9,180.\n - Point-of-sale terminals for Prescott (6 units), $7,494. Serial numbers\n   are on the invoice; the one that was stolen in the October break-in is\n   S/N TLY8840217735 (police report PPD 25-081144, insurance paid\n   $1,049 less deductible).\nGrant wants Section 179 on everything that qualifies. Your call.\n\n5. PREPAIDS AND LEASES\nStore leases unchanged except Flagstaff, which is owned by Hollingsworth Peak Properties, LLC\n-- that is Grant's brother Reid Hollingsworth. Rent went from $11,500 to\n$13,000 a month on July 1, 2025 with no written amendment. I have an email\nfrom Reid only. You will want this for the related-party note and for ASC 842.\nRelated: the company still carries a $60,000 note receivable from Grant\npersonally (the 2023 loan for the Lake Powell houseboat). No payments\nin 2025; interest accrued at 5%, $3,000.\n\n6. DEBT\nFour Peaks Commercial Finance:\n - Term loan no. 4410-229817, balance $318,744.02, matures 3/1/2029.\n - Van loan no. 4410-231005, balance $29,880.61.\n - Line of credit, limit $500,000, drawn $125,000 at year end.\nCovenant: debt service coverage 1.25x, tested annually. My calc is 1.31x\nbefore your adjustments, so there is not much room. Four Peaks needs\nreviewed statements by April 30, 2026. Their contact changed -- details\nare in the confirmation folder.\n\n7. PAYROLL AND ACCRUALS\nAccrued wages 5 days, $41,277. Accrued bonuses $52,000: Grant $25,000,\nme $12,000, three store managers $5,000 each. Paid 2/13/2026.\nTwo things HR asked me to keep out of the general ledger descriptions:\n - Paloma Guerrero-Stein (Sedona assistant manager, employee no. E-0217) has\n   been on FMLA leave since October 6 for chemotherapy. We are continuing\n   her health premium, $843.17 a month, and she owes her share, $212 a\n   month, which I have as a receivable of $636. Grant says forgive it.\n - DeShawn Carter (warehouse, E-0164) has a child support withholding order\n   from Maricopa County, case FC2019-052288, $388.50 per pay period.\n   December's second remittance went out late (1/6/2026).\nForm W-2 totals tie to the 941s. Company EIN is 86-0718834; state TPT\nlicense 21-448817 if you need it for the sales tax recon.\n\n8. CREDIT CARD\nCompany Amex ending 57838, December statement $19,206.77, coded and\naccrued. $2,140 of it is Grant's family trip to Telluride -- booked to\nshareholder distributions, not T&E. Winona Hollingsworth (Grant's wife, 10%\nshareholder) has a card on the same account; hers was clean.\n\n9. CONTINGENCIES -- PLEASE READ\n(a) Brittany Kowalski, the former Sedona store manager, was terminated\n9/26/2025 after the cycle counts showed the shrink in item 3. She filed\nan EEOC charge (540-2026-00412) on 12/11/2025 alleging pregnancy discrimination\nand retaliation; she also cites A.R.S. § 23-1501. Our employment lawyer is\nAurelio Benavidez of Benavidez Employment Law, PLC (602-555-0122). He says\nexposure is \"possible, not probable,\" range $40,000 to $90,000, insurance\nretention $25,000. Nothing accrued. He will answer your legal letter.\nMs. Kowalski has not been charged with anything and Grant does not\nwant the theft suspicion written anywhere it does not need to be.\n(b) Sales tax: Sedona city rate change was missed for six weeks. Under-\ncollected about $2,900. Accrued; amended return goes in with January.\n\n10. EQUITY / OTHER\nS-corp distributions $240,000 (Grant $216,000, Winona $24,000) plus the\nTelluride item. No new shareholders. Form 1120-S extension is fine with us\nif you need it.\n\n11. THINGS I THINK ARE FINE (so you do not spend time on them)\n - Gift cards: liability rolled forward by month, breakage recognized on the\n   same 24-month pattern as last year. No change in policy.\n - Loyalty points: accrued at the redemption value times the historical\n   redemption rate. The rate moved less than a point, so no true-up.\n - Returns reserve: Q4 sales were up, returns in the first three weeks of\n   January ran at the usual percentage, and I left the reserve formula alone.\n - Depreciation: ran all twelve months, agreed the schedule to the ledger,\n   and removed the stolen terminal and two fully depreciated display racks.\n - Prepaid insurance: the package policy renewed on the first of October and\n   is amortized straight-line over twelve months, nine remaining.\n - Sales tax payable other than item 9(b): agrees to the December returns as\n   filed for the state and all three cities.\n - Deferred revenue for guided trips: every booking with a trip date after\n   year end is deferred at the full deposit; the schedule is by trip.\n - Vacation accrual: recalculated from the timekeeping export at current\n   pay rates, capped at 80 hours per person as the handbook says.\n\n12. WHAT I NEED FROM YOU\n - A view on whether the legal matter in item 9(a) needs disclosure under\n   ASC 450 even though nothing is accrued. Grant will push back on any\n   wording that names a store.\n - The lease entry for the Flagstaff rent change. I can book it once you\n   tell me whether the email counts as a modification.\n - Whether the shareholder note in item 5 has to be reclassified out of\n   current assets, since nobody expects it to be repaid this year.\n - Your PBC list as early as possible. Last year it arrived the Friday\n   before fieldwork and we lost two days finding fixed asset invoices.\n - A draft of the covenant calculation in the lender's format before the\n   statements are issued, so there are no surprises.\n\nThat is the list. I am out February 2 for a minor procedure; Jordan can pull\ndocuments that day.\n\nRoz", "kind": "Text file", "detail": "1,313 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Hank Dellaria", "Lucinda Whitcombe", "Rosalyn Tsosie-Baker", "Paloma Guerrero-Stein", "DeShawn Carter", "Brittany Kowalski", "Grant", "Winona Hollingsworth", "Aurelio Benavidez", "Jordan", "Roz"], "companies": ["JUNIPER MESA OUTFITTERS, INC.", "Coconino Trail Runners Association", "Ponderosa National Bank", "Kaibab Credit Union", "Tallyho Payments", "Red Rock Guide Service L.L.C.", "Whitcombe Dellaria LLP", "Bergkamm Zelte GmbH", "Borgkamm", "Four Peaks Commercial Finance", "Hollingsworth Peak Properties, LLC", "Sedona", "Amex", "Benavidez Employment Law", "Maricopa County", "Flagstaff"]}, "topics": {"places": ["Ponderosa National Bank", "Coconino Trail Runners Association", "Kaibab Credit Union", "Tallyho Payments", "Flagstaff", "Sedona", "Prescott", "Hamburg", "Maricopa County", "Telluride"], "health": ["chemotherapy", "pregnancy discrimination", "retaliation", "procedure"], "sensitive": ["Chapter 7", "Reid Hollingsworth", "Grant", "Lake Powell houseboat", " EEOC charge", "criminal history"], "names": ["Hank", "Lucinda", "Rosalyn", "Jordan", "Brittany", "DeShawn", "Grant", "Winona", "Aurelio", "Roz"]}, "judged": {"candidates": 0, "requests": 0, "failures": 0, "places": [], "labels": {}}, "chunks": 5, "chunkErrors": 0, "topicErrors": 0, "importMs": 0.19999999552965164, "modelMs": 0, "topicMs": 0, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn", "bn_ca", "sin_ca", "ein", "card_partial", "phone", "street", "dob", "age90", "date", "passport_dl", "routing", "credential", "device", "vin", "record", "account", "m